<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Solving a disjoint compound inequality requiring an OR statement</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve each part of the following compound inequality:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle {@a@}x - {@b@} \le {@c@} \qquad \text{OR} \qquad {@d@}x + {@e@} > {@f@} \)
</p>
<p><i>(Enter the boundary values in the boxes below.)</i></p>
<p>\( x \le \) [[input:ans1]] &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>OR</b> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; \( x > \) [[input:ans2]]</p>

<div><b>First boundary:</b> [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<div><b>Second boundary:</b> [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>
<p>For an "OR" compound inequality, we solve each linear inequality completely separately.</p>

<p>First, we solve the left inequality:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
{@a@}x - {@b@} &\le {@c@} \\
{@a@}x &\le {@c@} + {@b@} \\
{@a@}x &\le {@c + b@} \\
x &\le \frac{{@c + b@}}{{@a@}} \\
x &\le {@ta1@}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>

<p>Next, we solve the right inequality:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
{@d@}x + {@e@} &> {@f@} \\
{@d@}x &> {@f@} - {@e@} \\
{@d@}x &> {@f - e@} \\
x &> \frac{{@f - e@}}{{@d@}} \\
x &> {@ta2@}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>

<p>Hence, the solution is the combination of both regions:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \boxed{x \le {@ta1@} \quad \text{OR} \quad x > {@ta2@}} \)
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
